From 807cac3d289bd0fd1119a7b2e3aff9787da01485 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:36:11 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Stack tab switcher: close-all undo, archiving off, incognito
 lock via Hub, model events, accessibility

- Close all tabs: do not close the model a second time without undo after
  the DISCARD_ALL animation; M153 commits pending closures there, which
  killed the Undo snackbar (tab loss).
- Tab archiving defaults to off while the stack serves HUB (phones
  without --disable-stack-tab-switcher); the stack has no "Inactive tabs"
  entry, and upstream rescues already-archived tabs on the next start.
- Incognito lock / accessibility: canUseStackLayout() decides (null
  profile, touch exploration, gesture-performing services -> Hub);
  exitStackIfUnusable() on resume and on accessibility changes leaves a
  stack that may no longer be shown, so the Hub with its lock view is
  used next. HubLayout is created even if the Hub manager already exists.
- Tabs created in the background or by code only get a card instead of
  closing the switcher; legacy willCloseTab/willCloseMultipleTabs remove
  cards for closes the stack did not start.
- Also drops the Safety Hub NTP magic-stack card registration left
  behind by Disable-safety-check (its delegate no longer exists).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
